IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Citizenship Act 2007 (Commonwealth) -- commencement and the old Act (ss 2, 4), permanent residence (s 5), citizenship
-- by birth (s 12), citizenship by descent (ss 16, 17, 19, 19A), and citizenship by conferral: general eligibility (s 21(2)), the
-- general residence requirement (s 22), the Minister's decision (s 24), the pledge of commitment (ss 25(3), 26) and the day
-- citizenship begins (s 28).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 37, compilation date 4 June 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 75, 2025"; register id C2026C00236),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2007A00020.txt (retrieved 2026-09-22).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0006 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl: priority 1, raised 8 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives (chloe c000, c062; jake k000, k051; daniel d000, d036, d040, d041). They ask: is a child born at KEMH or
-- Armadale Hospital a citizen by birth (s 12); is a child born in London to a citizen a citizen, and by what step (s 16); and what
-- residence does a partner-visa holder need before conferral, and what must she do (ss 21-22, 26). SCOPED to those provisions first,
-- with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them (ss 2, 4, 5, 17, 19, 19A, 24, 25(3), 28).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Australian Citizenship Act 1948, which s 4(2) and s 5(3) make decide any question about a time before 1 July 2007
-- (it is not deposited; its answers are INPUTS here); ss 7-8 (ships, posthumous births, artificial conception, surrogacy); ss 13-15
-- (adoption, abandoned children, incorporated territory); Subdivision AA (Hague adoptions); s 16(3) (births before 26 January
-- 1949); s 21(3)-(8) other than as a pledge exemption; the special residence and defence service requirements (ss 22A-23); the
-- citizenship test itself (s 23A and its determination, an INPUT); the national-security, identity and offence bars of ss 17 and 24
-- beyond their effect as one input; resumption (Subdivision C); renunciation, revocation and cessation (Division 3); evidence,
-- personal identifiers, review and the regulations (Parts 2 Div 4-5, Part 3). Fees are set under s 46 and the regulations (none
-- retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example encodings. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Australian Citizenship Act 2007`

§§ `2 and 4 -- commencement and the old Act`

-- s 2 table item 2: "Sections 2A to 54 ... A single day to be fixed by Proclamation" -- column 3: "1 July 2007 (see F2007L01653)".
-- s 3: "commencement day means the day on which sections 2A to 54 (as originally enacted) commence"; "old Act means the Australian
-- Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at any time before the commencement day".
-- s 4(2): "If, under this Act, it is necessary to work out if a person was an Australian citizen at a time before the commencement
-- day, work that out under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at that time." s 5(3) says the same of permanent
-- residence. Dates here are written YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `citizenship at that date is worked out under the 1948 Act` IF
    `the date` < 20070701

-- s 4(1): "Australian citizen means a person who: (a) is an Australian citizen under Division 1 or 2 of Part 2; or (b) satisfies both
-- of the following: (i) the person was an Australian citizen under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before the
-- commencement day; (ii) the person has not ceased to be an Australian citizen under this Act."
GIVEN `a citizen under Division 1 or 2 of Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a citizen under the 1948 Act immediately before 1 July 2007` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has ceased to be a citizen under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an Australian citizen under s 4(1)` IF
        `a citizen under Division 1 or 2 of Part 2`
    OR  (`a citizen under the 1948 Act immediately before 1 July 2007` AND (NOT `has ceased to be a citizen under this Act`))

§§ `5 -- permanent resident`

-- s 5(1): a person is a permanent resident at a particular time "if and only if: (a) the person is present in Australia at that time
-- and holds a permanent visa at that time; or (b) both: (i) the person is not present in Australia at that time and holds a
-- permanent visa at that time; and (ii) the person has previously been present in Australia and held a permanent visa immediately
-- before last leaving Australia; or (c) the person is covered by a determination in force under subsection (2) at that time."
GIVEN `present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `held a permanent visa in Australia immediately before last leaving` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `covered by a s 5(2) determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a permanent resident under s 5(1)` IF
        (`present in Australia` AND `holds a permanent visa`)
    OR  ((NOT `present in Australia`) AND `holds a permanent visa` AND `held a permanent visa in Australia immediately before last leaving`)
    OR  `covered by a s 5(2) determination`

§§ `12 -- citizenship by birth`

-- s 12(1): "A person born in Australia is an Australian citizen if and only if: (a) a parent of the person is an Australian citizen,
-- or a permanent resident, at the time the person is born; or (b) the person is ordinarily resident in Australia throughout the period
-- of 10 years beginning on the day the person is born."
-- s 12(2): "However, a person is not an Australian citizen under this section if, at the time the person is born: (a) a parent of the
-- person is an enemy alien; and (b) the place of the birth is under occupation by the enemy; unless, at that time, the other parent of
-- the person: (c) is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident; and (d) is not an enemy alien."
-- s 3: "child ... (a) an adopted child, stepchild or exnuptial child of the person". s 12 asks only for "a parent"; it has no
-- condition about the parents' marriage.
-- For a birth before 1 July 2007 the parent's status at the birth must itself be worked out under the 1948 Act (ss 4(2), 5(3)); it is
-- an INPUT here.
DECLARE `Birth facts` HAS
    `born in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent was a citizen or permanent resident at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in Australia for the 10 years from the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent was an enemy alien and the place of birth was under enemy occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other parent was a citizen or permanent resident and not an enemy alien` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `b` IS A `Birth facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen by birth under s 12` IF
        `b`'s `born in Australia`
    AND (`b`'s `a parent was a citizen or permanent resident at the birth` OR `b`'s `ordinarily resident in Australia for the 10 years from the birth`)
    AND (    (NOT `b`'s `a parent was an enemy alien and the place of birth was under enemy occupation`)
         OR  `b`'s `the other parent was a citizen or permanent resident and not an enemy alien`)

§§ `16, 17, 19 and 19A -- citizenship by descent`

-- s 16(1): "A person may make an application to the Minister to become an Australian citizen."
-- s 16(2): "A person born outside Australia on or after 26 January 1949 is eligible to become an Australian citizen if: (a) a parent of
-- the person was an Australian citizen at the time of the birth; and (b) if the parent was an Australian citizen under this
-- Subdivision or Subdivision AA, or section 10B, 10C or 11 of the old Act (about citizenship by descent), at the time of the birth:
-- (i) the parent has been present in Australia (except as an unlawful non-citizen) for a total period of at least 2 years at any time
-- before the person made the application; or (ii) the person is not a national or a citizen of any country at the time the person
-- made the application and the person has never been such a national or citizen; and (c) if the person is or has ever been a national
-- or a citizen of any country, or if article 1(2)(iii) of the Stateless Persons Convention applies to the person, and the person is
-- aged 18 or over at the time the person made the application -- the Minister is satisfied that the person is of good character at
-- the time of the Minister's decision on the application."
-- (The Stateless Persons Convention limb of (c) is not modelled.)
DECLARE `Descent facts` HAS
    `born outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of birth` IS A NUMBER
    `a parent was a citizen at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that parent was a citizen by descent at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that parent was lawfully present in Australia for 2 years in total before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has never been a national or citizen of any country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `of good character at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `d` IS A `Descent facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for citizenship by descent under s 16(2)` IF
        `d`'s `born outside Australia`
    AND `d`'s `date of birth` >= 19490126
    AND `d`'s `a parent was a citizen at the birth`
    AND (    (NOT `d`'s `that parent was a citizen by descent at the birth`)
         OR  `d`'s `that parent was lawfully present in Australia for 2 years in total before the application`
         OR  `d`'s `has never been a national or citizen of any country`)
    AND (    `d`'s `has never been a national or citizen of any country`
         OR  `d`'s `age at application` < 18
         OR  `d`'s `of good character at the decision`)

-- s 17(1A): the Minister "must not approve ... unless the person is eligible"; (2) "Subject to this section, the Minister must
-- approve the person becoming an Australian citizen if the person is eligible"; (3) not unless "satisfied of the identity of the
-- person"; (4)-(4B) security; (5) not within 12 months of ceasing to be a citizen. Unlike s 24(2), there is no power to refuse an
-- eligible applicant who clears the bars.
GIVEN `d` IS A `Descent facts`, `the Minister is satisfied of identity` IS A BOOLEAN, `a security or cessation bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must approve under s 17` IF
        `is eligible for citizenship by descent under s 16(2)` `d`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied of identity`
    AND (NOT `a security or cessation bar applies`)

-- s 19: "A person becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision on the day on which the Minister approves the person becoming
-- an Australian citizen." s 19A: "Despite section 19, a person does not become an Australian citizen under this Subdivision, even if
-- the Minister approves ..., unless: (a) if the person was born on or after 26 January 1949 -- a parent of the person was an
-- Australian citizen at the time of the person's birth". s 18: registration follows approval "in the manner prescribed by the
-- regulations"; it is not the step that makes the person a citizen.
GIVEN `d` IS A `Descent facts`, `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the approval date` IS A NUMBER, `the date asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen by descent on the date` IF
        `the Minister approved`
    AND `the date asked about` >= `the approval date`
    AND `d`'s `a parent was a citizen at the birth`

§§ `21(2) and 22 -- conferral: general eligibility and the general residence requirement`

-- s 22(1): the general residence requirement is met if "(a) the person was present in Australia for the period of 4 years immediately
-- before the day the person made the application; and (b) the person was not present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen at any
-- time during that 4 year period; and (c) the person was present in Australia as a permanent resident for the period of 12 months
-- immediately before the day the person made the application."
-- (1A): if "the total period of the absence or absences was not more than 12 months", the person "is taken to have been present in
-- Australia during each period of absence" -- so absences of MORE than 12 months save none of them.
-- (1B): for (1)(c), absences totalling "not more than 90 days", if "the person was a permanent resident during each period of
-- absence".
-- (1C): "taken not to satisfy paragraph (1)(a)" if confined in a prison, or in a psychiatric institution by court order in criminal
-- proceedings, at any time in the 4 years -- subject to the Minister's discretion in (5A).
-- (2): "Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply if the person: (a) was born in Australia; or (b) was an Australian citizen at any time
-- before the person made the application."
-- (5), (6): the Minister may treat a period PRESENT in Australia but not as a permanent resident (administrative error; significant
-- hardship) as one present as a permanent resident. (9), (11): the Minister may treat a period ABSENT from Australia while a permanent
-- resident as present as a permanent resident, for the spouse or de facto partner of a citizen (or one in an interdependent
-- relationship) who had "a close and continuing association with Australia during that period". (4A) (administrative error and
-- unlawful presence) is not modelled.
DECLARE `Conferral facts` HAS
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `a permanent resident at application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permanent resident at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a citizen before applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `absences in the 4 years before applying total more than 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an unlawful non-citizen in Australia during the 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `confined in prison or by court order during the 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister disapplies s 22(1C)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days present in the 12 months before applying not as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER
    `days absent in the 12 months before applying` IS A NUMBER
    `a permanent resident during every absence in those 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister treats the present days as permanent residence under s 22(5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `successfully completed the citizenship test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to reside in or keep a close association with Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of good character at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `present in Australia at the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bar under s 24(3), (4), (6) or (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A `Conferral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the 4 years of presence under s 22(1)(a)` IF
        (NOT `c`'s `absences in the 4 years before applying total more than 12 months`)
    AND (    (NOT `c`'s `confined in prison or by court order during the 4 years`)
         OR  `c`'s `the Minister disapplies s 22(1C)`)

GIVEN `c` IS A `Conferral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the 12 months as a permanent resident under s 22(1)(c)` IF
        (    `c`'s `days present in the 12 months before applying not as a permanent resident` = 0
         OR  `c`'s `the Minister treats the present days as permanent residence under s 22(5) or (6)`)
    AND (    `c`'s `days absent in the 12 months before applying` = 0
         OR  (`c`'s `days absent in the 12 months before applying` <= 90 AND `c`'s `a permanent resident during every absence in those 12 months`)
         OR  `c`'s `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)`)

GIVEN `c` IS A `Conferral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `satisfies the general residence requirement under s 22` IF
        (    `c`'s `born in Australia`
         OR  `c`'s `was a citizen before applying`
         OR  (`meets the 4 years of presence under s 22(1)(a)` `c` AND (NOT `c`'s `an unlawful non-citizen in Australia during the 4 years`)))
    AND `meets the 12 months as a permanent resident under s 22(1)(c)` `c`

-- s 21(2): eligible "if the Minister is satisfied that the person: (a) is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the application;
-- and (b) is a permanent resident: (i) at the time the person made the application; and (ii) at the time of the Minister's decision
-- ...; and (c) satisfies the general residence requirement ... at the time the person made the application; and (d) understands the
-- nature of an application ...; and (e) possesses a basic knowledge of the English language; and (f) has an adequate knowledge of
-- Australia and of the responsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship; and (g) is likely to reside, or to continue to
-- reside, in Australia or to maintain a close and continuing association with Australia ...; and (h) is of good character at the time
-- of the Minister's decision". (2A): (d), (e) and (f) "are taken to be satisfied if and only if" the person successfully completed an
-- approved test. The special residence and defence service routes in (c) are not modelled.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Conferral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for conferral under s 21(2)` IF
        `c`'s `age at application` >= 18
    AND `c`'s `a permanent resident at application`
    AND `c`'s `a permanent resident at the decision`
    AND `satisfies the general residence requirement under s 22` `c`
    AND `c`'s `successfully completed the citizenship test`
    AND `c`'s `likely to reside in or keep a close association with Australia`
    AND `c`'s `of good character at the decision`

§§ `24 -- the Minister's decision`

-- s 24(1A): "must not approve ... unless the person is eligible"; (2): "The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an
-- Australian citizen despite the person being eligible"; (3) identity; (4)-(4C) security; (6) pending proceedings, prison, parole
-- and recognizance periods; (7) 12 months after ceasing to be a citizen.
-- (5): if the person is covered by s 21(2), (3) or (4), has no special residence, "the Minister did not apply subsection 22(9)" and
-- "did not apply subsection 22(11)", "the Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian citizen at a time when the
-- person is not present in Australia."
-- Because of (2), the most this rule can say is that the Minister MAY approve.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Conferral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may approve under s 24` IF
        `is eligible for conferral under s 21(2)` `c`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `a bar under s 24(3), (4), (6) or (7) applies`)
    AND (`c`'s `present in Australia at the decision` OR `c`'s `the Minister applied s 22(9) or (11)`)

§§ `20, 25(3), 26 and 28 -- the pledge and the day citizenship begins`

-- s 26(1): "A person must make a pledge of commitment to become an Australian citizen unless the person: (a) is aged under 16 at the
-- time the person made the application ...; or (b) has a permanent or enduring physical or mental incapacity ...; or (c) is covered by
-- subsection 21(6), (7) or (8)."
GIVEN `age at application` IS A NUMBER, `has a s 26(1)(b) incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `covered by s 21(6), (7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must make a pledge of commitment` IF
        `age at application` >= 16
    AND (NOT `has a s 26(1)(b) incapacity`)
    AND (NOT `covered by s 21(6), (7) or (8)`)

-- s 26(2): "A person must not make a pledge of commitment before the Minister approves the person's application ... A pledge of
-- commitment made by the person before that time is of no effect." (3)-(6): the Minister may determine that the person cannot make the
-- pledge until the end of a specified period (not more than 12 months in total); a pledge made before then "is of no effect".
-- Write 0 for `the end of any s 26(3) delay` when no determination is in force.
GIVEN `the approval date` IS A NUMBER, `the pledge date` IS A NUMBER, `the end of any s 26(3) delay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pledge has effect` IF
        `the pledge date` >= `the approval date`
    AND `the pledge date` >= `the end of any s 26(3) delay`

-- s 20: "A person becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision if: (a) the Minister decides under subsection 24(1) to approve
-- ...; and (b) if the person is required to make a pledge of commitment ... the person makes that pledge."
-- s 28(1): a person required to pledge "becomes an Australian citizen under this Subdivision on the day on which the person makes the
-- pledge"; (2) otherwise "on the day on which the Minister approves". (s 28(3)-(4), children applying with a parent, not modelled.)
GIVEN `a pledge is required` IS A BOOLEAN, `the approval date` IS A NUMBER, `the pledge date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day citizenship by conferral begins` MEANS
    IF `a pledge is required` THEN `the pledge date` ELSE `the approval date`

-- s 25(1), (3): the Minister may cancel an approval if the person has not become a citizen and "has failed to make a pledge of
-- commitment within 12 months after the day on which the person received notice of the approval" for a reason not prescribed by the
-- regulations (the regulations were not retrieved; the reason is an INPUT). (5): a cancelled approval "is taken never to have been
-- given".
GIVEN `has become a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `pledged within 12 months of notice of approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `the reason is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approval may be cancelled for want of a pledge` IF
        (NOT `has become a citizen`)
    AND (NOT `pledged within 12 months of notice of approval`)
    AND (NOT `the reason is prescribed`)
